      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please don\u0027t be upset for the use of claude to analyze.  Each of the points raised are added as comments.  In summary:\n\n  Summary\n\n  The architectural intent is sound and the refactoring to get_plugin_manager() singleton is a clear improvement. The critical issue is the missing await\n  in notify.py that means dayzero will never fire at all. Beyond that, the run_mode feature is documented but not implemented, the tmux session name\n  collision will cause silent failures on re-allocated hosts, and the schedule query selects historical rather than current schedules.\n\nLeaving votes as neutral until various comments are addressed.",
      "revId": "3bd7e03700c722c478d67be5bfefd47a70cf2d99",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
