      "message": "4. README plugin examples have wrong execute() signature\n\n  The interface defines:\n  async def execute(self, cloud: str) -\u003e bool:\n\n  But the README documentation shows:\n  async def execute(self, host, cloud):   # both per_cloud and per_host examples\n\n  Any user who follows the README docs and implements execute(self, host, cloud) will get a TypeError at runtime because the dispatcher only passes\n  cloud. The built-in cloudcmd.py has the correct signature, but the docs contradict it.",
