      "message": "Significant\n\n  2. Hardcoded tmux session name will silently fail on repeat releases (cloudcmd.py:52)\n\n  tmux_cmd \u003d f\"tmux new-session -d -s quads_release \u0027echo {encoded} | base64 -d | bash\u0027\"\n\n  tmux new-session exits non-zero if a session named quads_release already exists. If a host gets re-allocated and the prior tmux session wasn\u0027t cleaned\n  up, the SSH command returns a non-zero exit code, _ssh_exec returns False, and the command is silently skipped. The session name should be unique per\n  invocation (e.g. include cloud name or a timestamp).",
      "revId": "3bd7e03700c722c478d67be5bfefd47a70cf2d99",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
