      "message": "8. Partial validation duplication in auth.py\n\n  auth.py:update_release_command manually re-implements length and control-character checks but does not call _validate_release_command(), which means\n  the blocked-patterns check (rm -rf, fork bomb, dd, mkfs, etc.) is not performed at the web layer. In practice the request goes through\n  quads.update_user() which hits the API and runs the full validation, so there\u0027s no actual security hole. But the duplicated partial logic in auth.py is\n  misleading and inconsistent - it will confuse future maintainers into thinking the web route is fully validating.",
      "revId": "3bd7e03700c722c478d67be5bfefd47a70cf2d99",
